<mxCell id="v614" value="The CDN price stays the same; the bill follows the bytes. Adaptive bitrate moves a viewer who cannot sustain 5 Mbps to the smaller rendition instead of stalling." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="270" width="820" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="v615" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; 375,000 GB ($7,500) vs 75,000 GB ($1,500). The codec and the bitrate ladder change the bill, not the CDN price." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="314" width="820" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
